  "notes": [
    "Schema checks structural constraints; typed decoding checks signed-64 range and cross-field consistency.",
    "Authority, relationships, current eligibility and receipt/dispatch transitions remain application service obligations.",
    "All registered operations now have concrete input/result candidates and explicit mode, authority, effect and recovery metadata. New query/command/completion envelopes coexist with earlier specialized candidate replies; no published SDK compatibility or production behavior claimed. Selection constraints must be applied before dispatch and before result publication.",
    "Each operation lists the schema revisions it negotiates (schemaRevisions). A request names one with the optional envelope member schemaRevision (absent means 1); <name>.rN.schema.json documents the shape at revision N and later and base documents are revision 1. Members introduced at N carry x-since N."
  ]
